id: E429
trigger_tool: runtime
phase: runtime
severity: 2
category: ohos, posix, threading, libc
match_keywords: QSharedMemory, shm_open, sem_open, AlreadyExists
title: POSIX shared memory and semaphore names collide in the tested OHOS runtime
error_signature: QSharedMemory::attach.*already exists|shm_same_name_create=-1 errno=17
root_cause: The tested runtime uses one object namespace for sem_open and shm_open. Qt creates a same-name internal semaphore before creating or attaching shared memory.
affected_scope: HarmonyOS PC HongMeng Kernel 1.12.0 HiShell runtime; Qt Base 6.11.1 POSIX native shared-memory keys
verification_cmd: Compile and run the self-contained native C reproducer in the paired document, then run tst_qsharedmemory with the candidate library.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: separate-internal-ipc-name
rec_description: Give the internal semaphore a distinct deterministic, bounded name while preserving the user-visible shared-memory key and locking.
rec_command: Apply qtbase/6.11.1.2 patch 0023 and execute the upstream shared-memory tests, retaining their assertions and adding ownership-based fixture cleanup.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: retain-failure-evidence
fallback_description: On a different runtime, reproduce both API orders and classify the actual namespace before choosing a naming convention.
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: disable.*systemsemaphore|ignore.*EEXIST
forbid_1_reason: Removing synchronization or treating collisions as success hides an invalid object mapping.
forbid_1_consequence: Data races or mapping a semaphore object as shared application memory.
principles: P003
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
